# Track D1 — Visual Baseline (Aligned Final Spec)

**Authors:** Claude + Codex (independent drafts cross-reviewed and aligned).
**Date:** 2026-04-20
**Status:** Final (design-only). Hand-off: Track D2 — implementation design.
**Scope:** Validates and trims the visual baseline at `doc/todo/frontend-ui-review/{README, design-tokens, motion-spec, roadmap}.md`. No code changes this round. No new visual direction — the baseline's "Tactile Intelligence" identity (Paper / Ink / Claw, Paw glyph, three-voice typography, breath motion) is the brand. This document is what survives a KISS pass.

> **KISS rule applied throughout.** Both reviewers explicitly rejected: golden-ratio spacing rationale, soft palette variants as named brand tokens, serif inside the live trace, persistent claw left rail on the chat row, typeset-receipt action card framing, hanging numerals on Settings, drawer naming metaphors ("// preferences" / "New entry"), edge-glow drift, Perlin-noise swipe, satellite tap ring, the 5-step shape ladder + 2 named specials, the `xxl = 52dp` spacing token, the `tgmTelegram` typography style, the `romanNumeral` typography style, the `PawStamp` shape token, and the 120sp Roman-numeral chapter watermarks.

---

## 1. Verdict

The baseline is **directionally right and tonally too loud**. The bones — Paper/Ink/Claw palette, three-voice typography, Paw glyph, 4-duration / 2-easing motion — are the brand and lock in unchanged. What gets cut is the themed flourishes that compete for attention (journal, telegram, ledger, chapter spread, receipt, fountain pen). The single consolidating principle: **the trace is the structure; everything else gets out of the way.**

Net diff vs baseline: roughly 30% of the surface area in `design-tokens.md` and `motion-spec.md` is removed or demoted. No new tokens. No new motion primitives.

